{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-939d4c008874f95a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9007\n3\ttitle: Bring-your-own vector database for RAG workloads\n4\tstatus: Refinement Done\n5\tpriority: Major\n6\tlabels:\n7\t- refined\n8\t- genai\n9\tlinks: []\n10\t---\n11\t\n12\t## Problem Statement\n13\t\n14\tRAG applications built on Llama Stack need a vector store, and today the\n15\tplatform neither ships one nor documents how to attach an external one.\n16\tCustomers are split into two camps with incompatible expectations: regulated\n17\tcustomers want a platform-managed vector database with supported images and\n18\tlifecycle, while cloud-native customers already run managed services (e.g.\n19\ta cloud vector DB) and only want a sanctioned way to connect them. We have not\n20\tdecided which posture to productize first, and the answer changes most of the\n21\tdownstream work.\n22\t\n23\t## High-Level Requirements\n24\t\n25\t| ID | Priority | Requirement |\n26\t|-------|----------|-------------|\n27\t| HLR-1 | P0 | A decision is reached, with a documented evaluation, on the first supported vector store posture: platform-managed (operator-deployed Milvus) versus external-connection-only. |\n28\t| HLR-2 | P0 | Depending on that decision: either administrators can deploy the managed vector store through the Platform Operator with productized images, or data scientists can register an external vector store connection per project with validated connectivity. |\n29\t| HLR-3 | P1 | Llama Stack distributions can consume the chosen vector store as a RAG provider without hand-editing distribution configs. |\n30\t| HLR-4 | P1 | The Dashboard exposes the chosen integration (deploy-and-manage UI for the managed path, or connection management UI for the external path). |\n31\t| HLR-5 | P2 | Product documentation covers setup and limits for whichever posture ships. |\n32\t\n33\t## Affected Components\n34\t\n35\t- Llama Stack\n36\t- Dashboard\n37\t- Platform Operator\n38\t\n39\t## Out of Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Shipping both postures in the same release\n42\t- Embedding model selection and lifecycle (separate strategy)\n43\t\n44\t## Open Questions\n45\t\n46\t1. Managed Milvus versus external-connection-only is genuinely undecided — the\n47\t   evaluation in HLR-1 must weigh supportability cost, disconnected-environment\n48\t   viability, and time-to-market, and the outcome forks the implementation\n49\t   structure for HLR-2 through HLR-5.\n50\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd31ab5e39a5836d","agent_id":"acab439dfc0167f5d","session_id":"6fdcac3b-4fd7-476b-9907-b8d1706b4a31","uuid":"542f90c8-6d99-446e-b838-937bcafce1ca","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:00:11.366Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-939d4c008874f95a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9007"}
