{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bed8c7bbc97fdf21","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9007\n3\tepic_count: 1\n4\tcritical_path_length: 5\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9007 (Bring-your-own vector database for RAG workloads)\n11\t\n12\t## Triage Outcome\n13\t\n14\tNeither Step 0 check fired. The strategy contains a single genuine unknown —\n15\twhich vector store posture to productize first (platform-managed,\n16\toperator-deployed Milvus vs external-connection-only) — and the strategy\n17\texplicitly states the answer \"forks the implementation structure for HLR-2\n18\tthrough HLR-5\". This is not a below-threshold strategy and not a docs-only\n19\tstrategy; it proceeds through full decomposition with a conditional\n20\t( two-branch ) structure.\n21\t\n22\t## Decomposition Structure\n23\t\n24\tThe main plan contains a single gating Investigation (E001) that resolves\n25\tHLR-1. Because the open question has exactly two bounded outcomes, the\n26\tdownstream work for HLR-2 through HLR-5 is expressed as conditional branch\n27\tepics:\n28\t\n29\t- **Branch A — platform-managed (operator-deployed Milvus)**: 7 epics\n30\t  (E002–E008 under the `BRANCH-A-` prefix)\n31\t- **Branch B — external-connection-only**: 4 epics\n32\t  (E002–E005 under the `BRANCH-B-` prefix)\n33\t\n34\tBranch epics are plan documents attached to the Investigation, not standalone\n35\tmain-plan nodes; the main-plan epic count is 1 and the main-plan-only critical\n36\tpath is 1. The summary frontmatter `critical_path_length` reports the\n37\t**effective delivery critical path** — the longest gate-to-completion path\n38\tacross the conditional branches — which is **5**: the posture decision, then\n39\tlicense validation, operator deployment, Llama Stack provider wiring, and\n40\tdocumentation (branch A; branch B's corresponding path is 4). Reporting the\n41\tmain-plan-only number (1) here would misrepresent the delivery timeline at a\n42\tglance, since all HLR-2 through HLR-5 work lives inside the branches.\n43\t\n44\t## Epic List\n45\t\n46\t### Main plan\n47\t\n48\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n49\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n50\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-E001 | Decide the first supported vector store posture (platform-managed vs external-connection-only) | Investigation | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n51\t\n52\t### Branch A — platform-managed (operator-deployed Milvus)\n53\t\n54\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n55\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n56\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E002 | Midstream repo onboarding for the Milvus vector database | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n57\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E003 | License validation for Milvus and transitive dependencies | Implementation (license-validation) | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n58\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E004 | Konflux build pipeline onboarding for the Milvus midstream image | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n59\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E005 | Platform Operator deployment and lifecycle for the managed vector store | Implementation | RHOAI Core | P0 |\n60\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E006 | Consume the managed vector store as a RAG provider in Llama Stack distributions | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | P1 |\n61\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E007 | Dashboard deploy-and-manage UI for the managed vector store | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n62\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E008 | Documentation for the platform-managed vector store posture | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n63\t\n64\t### Branch B — external-connection-only\n65\t\n66\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n67\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n68\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-B-E002 | Per-project external vector store connection registration with validated connectivity | Implementation | RHOAI Core | P0 |\n69\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-B-E003 | Consume registered external vector store connections as RAG providers in Llama Stack distributions | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | P1 |\n70\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-B-E004 | Dashboard connection management UI for external vector stores | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n71\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-B-E005 | Documentation for the external-connection-only vector store posture | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n72\t\n73\t## Dependency DAG\n74\t\n75\t```mermaid\n76\tgraph TD\n77\t    E001[E001 posture decision Investigation]\n78\t\n79\t    subgraph BranchA[Branch A - platform-managed]\n80\t        AE002[A-E002 Milvus repo-onboarding]\n81\t        AE003[A-E003 Milvus license-validation]\n82\t        AE004[A-E004 Milvus konflux-onboarding]\n83\t        AE005[A-E005 Operator managed Milvus deployment]\n84\t        AE006[A-E006 Llama Stack RAG provider wiring]\n85\t        AE007[A-E007 Dashboard deploy-and-manage UI]\n86\t        AE008[A-E008 managed-posture documentation]\n87\t        AE002 --> AE004\n88\t        AE003 --> AE005\n89\t        AE005 --> AE006\n90\t        AE005 --> AE007\n91\t        AE002 --> AE008\n92\t        AE003 --> AE008\n93\t        AE004 --> AE008\n94\t        AE005 --> AE008\n95\t        AE006 --> AE008\n96\t        AE007 --> AE008\n97\t    end\n98\t\n99\t    subgraph BranchB[Branch B - external-connection-only]\n100\t        BE002[B-E002 Operator connection registration]\n101\t        BE003[B-E003 Llama Stack provider wiring]\n102\t        BE004[B-E004 Dashboard connection UI]\n103\t        BE005[B-E005 external-posture documentation]\n104\t        BE002 --> BE003\n105\t        BE002 --> BE004\n106\t        BE002 --> BE005\n107\t        BE003 --> BE005\n108\t        BE004 --> BE005\n109\t    end\n110\t\n111\t    E001 --> AE002\n112\t    E001 --> AE003\n113\t    E001 --> AE004\n114\t    E001 --> AE005\n115\t    E001 --> AE006\n116\t    E001 --> AE007\n117\t    E001 --> AE008\n118\t    E001 --> BE002\n119\t    E001 --> BE003\n120\t    E001 --> BE004\n121\t    E001 --> BE005\n122\t```\n123\t\n124\tNote: the `E001 --> A-E004` edge is implied transitively via `A-E002`; it is\n125\tdrawn because every branch epic is gated by the Investigation (`gated_by`\n126\tmust be a member of `dependencies`). `A-E004` (konflux-onboarding) and\n127\t`A-E005` (operator implementation) have **no edge between them** by Rule 10 —\n128\tthey run in parallel, coupled only by a \"pinned image digest available\"\n129\tacceptance criterion.\n130\t\n131\t## DAG Justification\n132\t\n133\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n134\t|------|------|-----------|\n135\t| E001 → all branch epics | Rule 3 | The posture decision determines whether branch A or branch B epics exist at all. True gate: `remove` — if the other outcome is selected, this branch's epics are removed in favor of the other branch. Recorded via `gated_by` + `gate_failure_impact` on every branch epic. |\n136\t| A-E002 ∥ A-E003 (no edge) | Rule 7 | repo-onboarding and license-validation take independent inputs; parallel start. |\n137\t| A-E002 → A-E004 | Rule 5 | repo-onboarding → konflux-onboarding always serial; the build pipeline needs the repo. |\n138\t| A-E003 → A-E005 | Rule 9 | license-validation → general implementation serial; license failures change the dependency set and the approach. |\n139\t| A-E004 ∥ A-E005 (no edge) | Rule 10 | konflux-onboarding and the operator implementation are deliberately parallel. The operator consumes the productized Milvus image **digest** — a configuration reference (Rule 13 exception), enforced as a \"pinned image digest available\" AC on A-E005, never a DAG edge. |\n140\t| A-E002 ↛ A-E005 (no edge) | Rule 6 | repo-onboarding only serializes the implementation of the *onboarded* component's repo; the Platform Operator lives in a different repo and is not blocked. |\n141\t| A-E005 → A-E006 | Rules 12/13 | The Llama Stack distribution wiring builds against the connection surface the managed-deployment capability exposes (an API/CR, not a mere config value) — consuming Implementation is serial. |\n142\t| A-E005 → A-E007 | Rules 12/13 | The Dashboard UI builds against the same managed-deployment API/CR surface. |\n143\t| A-E008 blocked by all branch-A Implementations | Rule 11 | docs-authoring is always last; docs describe what was built. These edges do not trigger priority inheritance (docs-authoring priority exception). |\n144\t| B-E002 → B-E003 | Rules 12/13 | Llama Stack provider wiring builds against the connection-registration API/CR surface. |\n145\t| B-E002 → B-E004 | Rules 12/13 | Dashboard connection UI builds against the connection-registration API/CR surface. |\n146\t| B-E005 blocked by all branch-B Implementations | Rule 11 | docs-authoring always last within the branch. |\n147\t\n148\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n149\t\n150\t| HLR | Priority | Main-plan coverage | Branch A (managed) | Branch B (external) |\n151\t|-----|----------|--------------------|--------------------|---------------------|\n152\t| HLR-1 | P0 | E001 (Investigation) | — | — |\n153\t| HLR-2 | P0 | — | A-E002, A-E003, A-E004, A-E005 | B-E002 |\n154\t| HLR-3 | P1 | — | A-E006 | B-E003 |\n155\t| HLR-4 | P1 | — | A-E007 | B-E004 |\n156\t| HLR-5 | P2 | — | A-E008 | B-E005 |\n157\t\n158\tEvery HLR is covered in the main plan (HLR-1) or in **both** conditional\n159\tbranches (HLR-2 through HLR-5), matching the strategy's explicit conditional\n160\tphrasing (\"Depending on that decision\", \"the chosen vector store\", \"whichever\n161\tposture ships\"). No orphaned requirements.\n162\t\n163\tNote on HLR-5 priority: the docs epics are P1, not P2, because the\n164\t`docs-authoring` priority exception derives priority from the strategy\n165\tfrontmatter (`priority: Major` → P1) rather than from the P2 HLR.\n166\t\n167\t## Component & Team Mappings\n168\t\n169\t- **Milvus (vector database)** is not in `.context/rhai-components.txt` and has\n170\t  no architecture context file. Per the component-name constraint it is mapped\n171\t  to the closest parent-level canonical component **Llama Stack** (the RAG\n172\t  stack it serves), owned by **RHOAI GenAI**, for the provisioning epics\n173\t  (A-E002/A-E003/A-E004). The deployment epic (A-E005) is assigned to\n174\t  **Platform Operator** / **RHOAI Core** because the strategy makes the\n175\t  Platform Operator the deployment vehicle.\n176\t- **Platform Operator** is a canonical component but has **no architecture\n177\t  context file**, so its in-platform status could not be verified from the\n178\t  inventory. The strategy explicitly treats it as the existing deployment\n179\t  vehicle (\"deploy … through the Platform Operator\"), so it is treated as\n180\t  in-platform rather than generating a provisioning chain; see Health\n181\t  Warnings. Owner team **RHOAI Core** is assumed (the strategy provides no\n182\t  Impacted Teams table).\n183\t- **Documentation** epic team assumed **RHOAI Documentation** (no team table\n184\t  in strategy).\n185\t- **Llama Stack** → RHOAI GenAI and **Dashboard** → RHOAI Dashboard per their\n186\t  architecture context files.\n187\t\n188\t## New Component Detection (Step 2)\n189\t\n190\t- **Milvus**: not in architecture context → full onboarding chain generated\n191\t  per Rule 20 for branch A: `repo-onboarding` (A-E002) + `license-validation`\n192\t  (A-E003) parallel start → `konflux-onboarding` (A-E004, after repo) →\n193\t  consumed by the operator implementation (A-E005, after license-validation;\n194\t  parallel with konflux). No separate Investigation epic for dependency\n195\t  availability: Milvus is an established OSS project with a public upstream,\n196\t  so availability is not in doubt — only posture is, and that is E001's scope.\n197\t- **Branch B** provisions no new component: it connects to externally operated\n198\t  stores, so no onboarding chain applies.\n199\t\n200\t## Staff Engineer Input\n201\t\n202\tNone present in the strategy — no overrides to log.\n203\t\n204\t## Health Warnings\n205\t\n206\t1. **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): the strategy has no Impacted\n207\t   Teams table, no Dependencies table, no formal Given/When/Then Acceptance\n208\t   Criteria, and no Non-Functional Requirements. Teams were inferred from\n209\t   architecture context (Llama Stack → RHOAI GenAI, Dashboard → RHOAI\n210\t   Dashboard) and assumed for Platform Operator (RHOAI Core) and\n211\t   Documentation (RHOAI Documentation). Epic acceptance criteria were derived\n212\t   from HLR text rather than strategy ACs.\n213\t2. **Platform Operator lacks an architecture context file** (non-blocking\n214\t   scope watch): per the platform-inventory rule it is not verifiably \"in the\n215\t   platform\". Because the strategy asserts it as the existing deployment\n216\t   vehicle, it was decomposed as an existing component rather than generating\n217\t   a Rule 20 provisioning chain for the operator itself. If the operator's\n218\t   extension surface does not support third-party stateful components, branch\n219\t   A's A-E005 scope grows — verify during implementation. Signal 9\n220\t   (architecture_claims) is scored -1 on Platform Operator epics for this\n221\t   reason.\n222\t3. **Docs priority vs HLR-5**: HLR-5 is P2 in the strategy, but docs epics\n223\t   carry P1 per the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy frontmatter\n224\t   `priority: Major` → P1). Flagged so the reviewer does not read it as a\n225\t   priority inversion.\n226\t4. **Stateful storage scope trap** (watch, not a flag): the managed posture\n227\t   implies operator-managed persistent storage for Milvus. The strategy's\n228\t   NFRs are absent, so storage sizing/limits are left as implementation\n229\t   scope; A-E008 (docs) must document limits explicitly per HLR-5.\n230\t\n231\t## Tiered Delivery\n232\t\n233\tNot applicable in the Rule-16/17 sense: there is no external dependency with\n234\tuncertain timing (Milvus is OSS productized by us; external stores in branch\n235\tB are customer-operated). The strategy-level fork is handled by conditional\n236\tbranches instead: no partial user value is deliverable before the posture\n237\tdecision (HLR-2 through HLR-5 are all posture-conditional), so E001 gates all\n238\tdownstream work. Within each branch, work proceeds in parallel per the DAG\n239\tabove.\n240\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99d8eb620e547779","agent_id":"ac7fe1d2a48a6c62c","session_id":"6fdcac3b-4fd7-476b-9907-b8d1706b4a31","uuid":"7b590f56-c2b9-42c1-8f41-90d9e2100e57","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:24:31.686Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bed8c7bbc97fdf21","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9007"}
